# Supabase local/NAS test stack (BACKLOG-3114)
# baseline-*.sql is a pg_dump of production's schema. This repo is PUBLIC and the
# file is one `git add .` from exposure; it lives at ~/.keepr/db-baseline/ instead.
# `baseline*.sql` covers BOTH the dated name and the plain `supabase/baseline.sql`
# that an earlier instruction on BACKLOG-3114 told the founder to dump to; the
# `*.sql` line is the net for any other name (`prod-schema.sql`, ...). Nothing is
# tracked at this depth -- every committed .sql lives under migrations/, seed/ or
# tests/ -- so this ignores dumps without hiding anything real.
supabase/baseline*.sql
supabase/*.sql
# `supabase link` writes the linked project ref and version pins here;
# `supabase start` writes .branches/. Neither belongs in the repo.
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/

# BACKLOG-2553: esbuild bundle of the contact worker, built and removed by
